{"type":"frame","id":"Znh8i","x":0,"y":12839,"name":"Screen/Docs — FAQ","theme":{"H:Mode":"Dark"},"clip":true,"width":1440,"height":900,"fill":"$H:--background","children":[{"id":"vZ7kK","type":"ref","ref":"K2Rt4H","height":"fill_container","name":"DocsSidebar/Expanded","width":280},{"type":"frame","id":"d9nRU1","name":"Main","width":"fill_container","height":"fill_container","fill":"$H:--background","layout":"vertical","children":[{"id":"cBBSQ","type":"ref","ref":"SOdlr","name":"Docs Top Bar","width":"fill_container","descendants":{"NImey":{"content":"Reference"},"ikbi6":{"content":"FAQ"}}},{"type":"frame","id":"Rmjt1","name":"Body","clip":true,"width":"fill_container","height":"fill_container","layout":"vertical","gap":16,"padding":32,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"czwgP","fill":"$H:--primary","content":"DOCUMENTATION","fontFamily":"$H:--font-primary","fontSize":12,"fontWeight":"600"},{"type":"text","id":"ygXf4","fill":"$H:--foreground","content":"Frequently Asked Questions","fontFamily":"$H:--font-primary","fontSize":32,"fontWeight":"700"},{"type":"text","id":"GgJ13","fill":"$H:--muted-foreground","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":700,"content":"Common questions before you deploy Gameplane to your cluster.","fontFamily":"$H:--font-secondary","fontSize":16,"fontWeight":"normal"},{"type":"frame","id":"d9OBmF","width":"fill_container","gap":32,"children":[{"type":"frame","id":"jfw6L","width":"fill_container","layout":"vertical","gap":16,"children":[{"type":"frame","id":"SnzjF","width":"fill_container","layout":"vertical","gap":4,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"bf9ym","fill":"$H:--foreground","content":"Do I need to know Kubernetes?","fontFamily":"$H:--font-primary","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"600"},{"type":"text","id":"ANhU4","fill":"$H:--muted-foreground","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":"fill_container","content":"One-time cluster setup benefits from basic Helm familiarity. Day-to-day server management — console, files, backups, players — is entirely dashboard-driven; kubectl is optional.","lineHeight":1.5,"fontFamily":"$H:--font-secondary","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"normal"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"x0tsnt","width":"fill_container","layout":"vertical","gap":4,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"D8m6ZT","fill":"$H:--foreground","content":"Is Gameplane production-ready?","fontFamily":"$H:--font-primary","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"600"},{"type":"text","id":"vmvVd","fill":"$H:--muted-foreground","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":"fill_container","content":"It's in beta (v0.2.0-beta.7). Core workflows are feature-complete and tested, but not yet recommended for unattended production — see the Roadmap.","lineHeight":1.5,"fontFamily":"$H:--font-secondary","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"normal"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"MovBr","width":"fill_container","layout":"vertical","gap":4,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"Qmybr","fill":"$H:--foreground","content":"Is it free?","fontFamily":"$H:--font-primary","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"600"},{"type":"text","id":"MSHM9","fill":"$H:--muted-foreground","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":"fill_container","content":"Yes. Gameplane is open-source under AGPL-3.0-or-later, with no paid tiers.","lineHeight":1.5,"fontFamily":"$H:--font-secondary","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"normal"}]}]},{"type":"frame","id":"U5LykJ","width":"fill_container","layout":"vertical","gap":16,"children":[{"type":"frame","id":"t3lNa1","width":"fill_container","layout":"vertical","gap":4,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"PWXT9","fill":"$H:--foreground","content":"What happens to my data if I uninstall?","fontFamily":"$H:--font-primary","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"600"},{"type":"text","id":"uTWW3","fill":"$H:--muted-foreground","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":"fill_container","content":"Depends on your cluster's StorageClass reclaim policy — Gameplane doesn't force-delete PVCs itself. Back up critical data before uninstalling.","lineHeight":1.5,"fontFamily":"$H:--font-secondary","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"normal"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"yuE2x","width":"fill_container","layout":"vertical","gap":4,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"bGbwW","fill":"$H:--foreground","content":"What database does it use?","fontFamily":"$H:--font-primary","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"600"},{"type":"text","id":"q1SHgn","fill":"$H:--muted-foreground","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":"fill_container","content":"SQLite by default and is the production-tested driver. A PostgreSQL driver exists but is experimental (build-tag-gated, work in progress).","lineHeight":1.5,"fontFamily":"$H:--font-secondary","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"normal"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"K9jX1E","width":"fill_container","layout":"vertical","gap":4,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"NvXnf","fill":"$H:--foreground","content":"Can I manage servers without the dashboard?","fontFamily":"$H:--font-primary","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"600"},{"type":"text","id":"g0bJb4","fill":"$H:--muted-foreground","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":"fill_container","content":"Yes. Advanced users can bypass the API entirely and manage everything with kubectl apply — the operator is authoritative, so both stay in sync.","lineHeight":1.5,"fontFamily":"$H:--font-secondary","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"normal"}]}]}]},{"type":"frame","id":"wYaZG","name":"PrevNext","width":"fill_container","stroke":"$H:--border","strokeWidth":{"top":1},"strokeAlignment":"inner","strokeLinejoin":"round","padding":[16,0,0,0],"justifyContent":"space_between","alignItems":"center","children":[{"type":"frame","id":"uz9ii","gap":6,"alignItems":"center","children":[{"type":"icon","id":"cFh5M","width":14,"height":14,"icon":"arrow-left","library":"lucide","fill":"$H:--muted-foreground"},{"type":"frame","id":"Mu4bK","layout":"vertical","children":[{"type":"text","id":"f88ljD","fill":"$H:--muted-foreground","content":"Previous","fontFamily":"$H:--font-secondary","fontSize":11,"fontWeight":"normal"},{"type":"text","id":"wNmbs","fill":"$H:--foreground","content":"Roadmap","fontFamily":"$H:--font-prim